  "description": "AGSC-08-15 (amended 2026-10-02 for 1.0.0): every shape of the minimum set is detected and nothing outside it is. Each string is the concatenation of its `parts`, so that no file of the distribution carries a credential- or number-shaped string a secret scanner would flag; it is checked alone, as one in-scope string of an item; `code` is the code reported for it, or null when the string raises nothing. The positive strings are one per private-key block, provider prefix and assignment form the rule lists; every token is visibly fake (one repeated character) and only as long as the rule's minimum. The negative strings are the placeholders the rule names, a value under eight characters, a prefix named in prose, and tokens one character short of the rule's length. Derived by hand from the rule text; how many findings one string raises is not asserted.",
